# {{NAME}} — Fusion 360 Add-in

{{DESCRIPTION}}

## Installation

1. Download or `git clone` this repository.
2. In Fusion 360 go to **Utilities** tab → **Scripts and Add-Ins** (or press Shift+S).
3. Switch to the **Add-Ins** tab.
4. Click the green **+** ("Add existing script or add-in").
5. Browse to the `{{NAME}}` folder (the inner folder containing
   `{{NAME}}.py`) and select it.
6. Select **{{NAME}}** in the list and click **Run**.
   Optionally check **Run on Startup**.

The button appears in a **{{PANEL_NAME}}** panel on the **Utilities** tab and in
**Solid → Create**.

## Usage

Open (or create) a design and click **{{COMMAND_NAME}}**. Nothing has to be
selected or modeled first: the add-in creates a **new component** under the
active component, in a fixed frame (origin at the part's front-left top
corner, length along +X, top face on the XY plane). Move or joint the
component to place it.

The **Start from** dropdown at the top of the dialog decides which values you
begin with: your previous run's values (default), the add-in defaults, or an
existing layout of this document — which loads its parameters back and
rebuilds it in place on OK.

All values accept any unit (`25.5 in`, `648 mm`). The info box at the bottom
shows a live sanity readout and any validation problem. Last-used values are
remembered in `{{NAME}}/settings.json` (created automatically).

## Development

```
{{NAME}}/                        # the folder you install in Fusion
├── {{NAME}}.py                  # entry: toolbar registration, run()/stop()
├── {{NAME}}.manifest
├── {{NAME}}Command.py           # the command: dialog, validation, build
├── {{MATH_MODULE}}.py           # pure-python geometry math (no adsk)
├── constants.py                 # attribute names, metadata version
├── Fusion360Utilities/          # verbatim command-framework template (MIT)
└── resources/{{CMD_SLUG}}/      # toolbar icons (16/32 px + disabled)
tests/test_{{MATH_MODULE}}.py    # pytest suite for the math
scripts/make_icons.py            # icon generator (pure stdlib PNG writer)
```

- The math is pure Python; test it without Fusion: `python -m pytest tests/`.
- Toolbar icons are generated by
  `python scripts/make_icons.py {{NAME}}/resources/{{CMD_SLUG}}`
  (pass `--glyph my_glyph.txt`, 16 lines of 16 characters with `#` as ink,
  for a custom glyph).
- API assumptions worth re-verifying on new Fusion releases are listed in
  [DEV_NOTES.md](DEV_NOTES.md); the feature history is in
  [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md).
- Command skeleton based on the `Fusion360Utilities` helpers from
  [Fusion360AddinSkeleton](https://github.com/tapnair/Fusion360AddinSkeleton)
  by Patrick Rainsberry (MIT).
